BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:American Zoo 🎟️
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261013T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261013T210000
DTSTAMP:20260916T171252Z
UID:6a85e6f6eb5b7ddb41ae0ca0@woodstockfilmfestival.org
DESCRIPTION:Community Presenter:The Overlook News\n\nThe 27th Annual Woods
 tock Film Festival kicks off with the Hudson Valley premiere ofAmerican Zo
 o. The post-screening Q&A features director Tim Travers Hawkins and specia
 l guests\, moderated by Noah Eckstein\, founding editor-in-chief ofThe Ove
 rlook News.\n\nAbout the Film:Every documentary filmmaker dreams of findin
 g a lost archive and hidden history. WithAmerican Zoo\, director Tim Trave
 rs Hawkins found both. This gripping film unravels the hidden history of a
  beloved local attraction – the Catskill Game Farm – and the complex b
 ond between humans and animals. – Jessica Edwards\n\nTim Travers Hawkins
  is an Emmy-nominated documentary filmmaker known for cinematic and invest
 igative nonfiction exploring systems of power\, justice and institutional 
 accountability. His debut feature\,XY Chelsea\, premiered at the 2019 Trib
 eca Film Festival and earned two Documentary Emmy Award nominations. His o
 ther work includesThe MovementforThe Guardian\,Personafor HBO Max\,Burn It
  Down!for Paramount andCapturing the Killer Nursefor Netflix. Hawkins stud
 ied filmmaking at EICTV in Cuba and trained in Latin America with filmmake
 rs Fernando Birri and Pino Solanas. His latest feature documentary\,Americ
 an Zoo\, had its World Premiere at the 2026 Tribeca Festival.\n\nNoah Ecks
 tein is the founding editor-in-chief ofThe Overlook\, a nonprofit news out
 let providing public-service journalism across seven towns in the Catskill
 s. His work has appeared inThe New York Times\,Vogue\,Semafor\,Variety\,Th
 e GuardianandFast Company\, among other national and international publica
 tions.\n\n🎟️ Tickets Available\n\n🔗 https://woodstockfilmfestival.
 org/2026-all-events?eventId=6a85e6f6eb5b7ddb41ae0ca0
LOCATION:The Community Theatre\, 373 Main St\, Catskill\, NY 12414
URL:https://woodstockfilmfestival.org/2026-all-events?eventId=6a85e6f6eb5b
 7ddb41ae0ca0
END:VEVENT
