BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:MASTERCLASS WITH ROGER ROSS WILLIAMS\, JULIE GOLDMAN & CHRISTOPHER
  CLEMENTS:  Finding the film’s voice: The creative collaboration between
  director and producer 🎟️
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261016T094500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261016T114500
DTSTAMP:20260922T175058Z
UID:6aadb44829e60021bfe933a0@woodstockfilmfestival.org
DESCRIPTION:In this conversation\, director Roger Ross Williams and produc
 ers Julie Goldman and Christopher Clements draw from their years of collab
 oration to explore the director-producer relationship\, from developing a 
 shared creative vision to navigating challenges throughout production. Thr
 ough stories and case studies from their work together\, they will discuss
  how responsibilities are divided\, how creative differences are addressed
 \, and how ongoing communication and trust can help overcome the creative 
 and practical challenges of filmmaking.\n\nPanelists:\n\nRoger Ross Willia
 ms\n\nJulie Goldman\n\nChristopher Clements\n\nPanelists:\n\nRoger Ross Wi
 lliamsis an Oscar®\, Emmy\, Peabody\, and NAACP Image Award-winning direc
 tor\, producer\, and writer – and the first African American director to
  win an Academy Award\, with his filmMusic By Prudence. Williams directedL
 ife\, Animated\, which won him the Sundance Directing Award\, and was nomi
 nated for an Academy Award ® and won three Emmys. Williams is the recipie
 nt of the Career Achievement Award from the International Documentary Asso
 ciation\, The Woodstock Film Festival Maverick Award\, The NYU Alumni Achi
 evement Award\, and an honorary doctorate from Lafayette College. His prod
 uction company One Story Up produced the acclaimed food seriesHigh On The 
 Hog\, an adaptation of Ta-Nehisi Coates'sBetween The World And Me\, the Be
 n Crump documentaryCivil\, the award-winning filmMaster Of Light\, and the
  Primetime Emmy award-winning feature documentaryThe Apollo. Williams' fir
 st scripted featureCassandrofrom Amazon Prime Video had its World premiere
  at the 2023 Sundance Film Festival to universal acclaim. He also released
 The Supermodelsfor Apple TV+\, Oscar Shortlisted DocumentaryStamped From T
 he Beginning\, based on the book by Ibram X. Kendi\, for Netflix\, and the
  Emmy award-winning seriesThe 1619 Projectfor Disney/Hulu.  Williams is c
 urrently working on his next project\, the narrative featureStrange Arriva
 ls\, starring Demi Moore and Colman Domingo.\n\nJULIE GOLDMAN – PRODUCER
 \, MOTTO PICTURES\n\nJulie Goldman is an Oscar®-nominated and Emmy Award-
 winning producer and executive producer of documentary and fiction films\,
  and series. Julie is the first documentary producer to receive the Amazon
  Studios Sundance Institute Producer’s Award and the Cinereach Producer
 ’s Award. She recently producedSelena y Los Dinos\, which premiered at S
 undance and won the U.S. Documentary Special Jury Award\, in addition to A
 udience Awards at SXSW and Miami Film Festivals. In 2023\, three of her fi
 lms premiered at Sundance: the Emmy-winningVictim/Suspect\, the Grand Jury
  Prize-winning and Oscar-NominatedThe Eternal Memory\, and Roger Ross Will
 iams’ acclaimed fiction featureCassandro\, starring Gael Garcia Bernal a
 nd featuring Bad Bunny. Julie produced Nanfu Wang’s Peabody-Award winnin
 g and Oscar-shortlistedIn the Same Breath\; Todd Haynes’The Velvet Under
 ground\; the Peabody and Emmy Awards winnerA Thousand Cuts\;The Return of 
 Tanya Tucker: Featuring Brandi Carlile\; and the Oscar-nominated filmsLife
 \, AnimatedandAbacus: Small Enough to Jail. She executive produced the Osc
 ar-nominatedThe Mole Agentand the Sundance Grand Jury Prize- winningWeiner
 . Julie’s current slate includes the third season of the hit Netflix ser
 iesA Man on the Insidestarring Ted Danson\, and new films from directors i
 ncluding Maite Alberdi\, Roger Ross Williams\, Kathlyn Horan\, and Marcus 
 Lindeen.\n\nCHRISTOPHER CLEMENTS – PRODUCER\, MOTTO PICTURES\n\nChristop
 her Clements is an Emmy and Peabody Award-winning producer and partner at 
 Motto Pictures. He recently producedSelena y Los Dinos\, which premiered a
 t Sundance this year and won the U.S. Documentary Special Jury Award for A
 rchival Storytelling\, and received an Audience Award at SXSW. He produced
  the Emmy-winningVictim/Suspect\,and executive producedCassandrostarring G
 ael Garcia Bernal and featuring Bad Bunny\, and the Grand Jury Prize-winni
 ngThe Eternal Memory\, all of which premiered at the 2023 Sundance Film Fe
 stival. Christopher producedAmerican Pain\;Unfinished Business\;The Return
  of Tanya Tucker: Featuring Brandi Carlile\,which won the SXSW Film Festiv
 al Audience Award\; the Peabody and DuPont Award-winningIn the Same Breath
 \; Todd Haynes’ Oscar-shortlistedThe Velvet Underground\; and the Peabod
 y and Emmy-winningA Thousand Cuts\,which followed journalists in the Phili
 ppines led by Nobel Prize winner Maria Ressa. He executive produced the Ac
 ademy Award-nominatedThe Mole AgentandAbacus: Small Enough to Jail\; the O
 scar-shortlistedWeiner\; the Peabody Award-winningInventing TomorrowandSou
 thwest of Salem\, which directly contributed to the legal appeal that exon
 erated four falsely accused and long imprisoned women in Texas. Christophe
 r’s current slate includes the third season of Mike Schur’ hit Netflix
  seriesA Man on the Insidestarring Ted Danson\, which is based onThe Mole 
 Agent\, and new films from directors including Maite Alberdi\, Roger Ross 
 Williams\, Kathlyn Horan and Marcus Lindeen.\n\n🎟️ Tickets Available
 \n\n🔗 https://woodstockfilmfestival.org/2026-all-events?eventId=6aadb44
 829e60021bfe933a0
LOCATION:Utopia Studios\, 293 Tinker Street\, Woodstock\, NY 12498
URL:https://woodstockfilmfestival.org/2026-all-events?eventId=6aadb44829e6
 0021bfe933a0
