UID:6aad4892db7fedeaf774440e@woodstockfilmfestival.org
DESCRIPTION:ABOUT THE FILM:\n\nIn the occupied West Bank\, Palestinian com
 munities face escalating settler violence and ongoing attempts to displace
  them. Israeli activists\, armed only with their cellphones\, stand in sol
 idarity with them\, documenting attacks\, trying to fend off intruders and
  standing beside them as they struggle to remain on their land.\n\nABOUT T
 HE FILMMAKER:\n\n﻿Hilla Medaliais an Academy Award®-nominated and Peabo
 dy Award-winning documentary director and producer whose work is recognize
 d worldwide for its emotional depth\, cultural insight\, and narrative bol
 dness. She has received six Emmy nominations for her films\, and her proje
 cts have screened internationally in theaters and on major platforms\, inc
 luding HBO\, MTV\, PBS\, BBC\, ARTE\, and Netflix. She is a member of the 
 Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences\, the Producers Guild of Ameri
 ca\, and holds an M.A. in Film and Television from Southern Illinois Unive
 rsity.\n\n🎟️ Tickets Available\n\n🔗 https://woodstockfilmfestival.
 org/2026-all-events?eventId=6aad4892db7fedeaf774440e
LOCATION:Tinker Street Cinema\, 132 Tinker Street\, Woodstock\, NY 12498
URL:https://woodstockfilmfestival.org/2026-all-events?eventId=6aad4892db7f
 edeaf774440e
END:VEVENT
