BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:GRILLING BILL PLYMPTON 🎟️
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261016T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261016T163000
DTSTAMP:20260922T185225Z
UID:6a98633470ce680e3ee7ac2f@woodstockfilmfestival.org
DESCRIPTION:ABOUT THE SPECIAL EVENT:\n\n﻿To celebrate Bill Plympton’s 
 milestone 80th birthday and to let audiences peek behind the scenes of mak
 ing some of his shorts\, a fellow independent animator Signe Baumane will 
 grill Bill to keep him humble. Together they will screen some of Bill’s 
 shorts and discuss secrets of Bill’s long and successful career.\n\nThey
  will try to pin down the mysterious place where creativity comes from and
  elaborate on why artists are the Cassandras of our times.\n\nFeaturing:Yo
 ur Face\, Homer's Face\, Guard Dog\, Mexican Standoff\, Nose Hair\, Duckvi
 lle\, The Cow Who Wanted to be a Hamburger\, Santa the Fascist Years\, Wha
 le 52.\n\nABOUT THE FILMMAKERS:\n\nBill Plymptonis the most influential in
 dependent animator that has ever lived. He has been nominated for an Oscar
 ® two times\, has made over 120 shorts and feature films\, impacted thous
 ands of careers and has worked with recognizable name such as Whoopi Goldb
 erg\, Kanye West\, Matthew Modine\, Paul Giamatti among many.\n\nSigne Bau
 maneis a Latvian born\, Brooklyn-based independent filmmaker\, artist\, wr
 iter\, and animator. She has made seventeen award-winning animated shorts.
  Her first animated featureRocks in My Pockets(2014) screened at over 130 
 international festivals and opened theatrically in the U.S. through Zeitge
 ist Films. Signe’s second animated featureMy Love Affair with Marriage(2
 022)\, tells the story of a spirited young woman’s quest for perfect lov
 e and lasting marriage. It premiered at Tribeca Festival\, screened at 110
  festivals\, winning 25 awards\, and was released theatrically in North Am
 erica through 8 Above. She is now working on her third animated featureKar
 mic Knot(2028). Signe is a Guggenheim Fellow and has a degree in Philosoph
 y from Moscow State University.\n\n🎟️ Tickets Available\n\n🔗 https
 ://woodstockfilmfestival.org/2026-all-events?eventId=6a98633470ce680e3ee7a
 c2f
LOCATION:Woodstock Playhouse\, 103 Mill Hill Rd\, Woodstock\, NY 12498
URL:https://woodstockfilmfestival.org/2026-all-events?eventId=6a98633470ce
 680e3ee7ac2f
END:VEVENT
