BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LIVE PODCAST WITH AMY HOBBY & AVI ZEV WEIDER: FEATURING MARK DUPLA
 SS & KATIE ASELTON 🎟️
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T120000
DTSTAMP:20260917T175212Z
UID:6aa1be2c843a0b27c5b431cf@woodstockfilmfestival.org
DESCRIPTION:Every filmmaker carries with them the ghosts of films that nev
 er came to be — the abandoned scripts\, impossible casting dreams\, proj
 ects that collapsed in financing\, or stories that proved simply too stran
 ge\, ambitious\, or ahead of their time to make.. Through conversation\, a
 rchival development materials\, and speculative reimaginings\, the series 
 revisits the unrealized films that continue to haunt their creators and as
 ks what those unfinished works can still reveal about artistic ambition\, 
 industry gatekeeping\, and the creative process itself. Part confessional
 \, part creative autopsy\, and part speculative resurrection\,Films Not Ma
 deoffers a rare glimpse into the hidden archive of cinema: the stories tha
 t almost were — and the unfinished ideas that continue to shape the ones
  that get made. In this special live recording of the podcast\, hosts Amy 
 Hobby and Avi Zev Weider invite a filmmaker into a candid excavation of a 
 project they couldn’t quite bring to life.\n\nPanelists:\n\nMark Duplass
 is an actor\, filmmaker\, and producer known for his roles inThe Morning S
 howandTogetherness. Co-founder of Duplass Brothers Productions\, he has ma
 ny award winning independent films\, hit series\, and documentary films an
 d series. Notable credits includeThe Puffy Chair\,Somebody Somewhere\, and
 Wild Wild Country.\n\nKatie Aseltonis an acclaimed actor and filmmaker wor
 king across television and film. Her breakout acting role was in the indie
  hitThe Puffy Chair\, directed by Mark and Jay Duplass\, Directing credits
  includeBlack Rock\,Mack And Rita\,Magic Hour\, and - most recently -Their
  Town.\n\nModerators:\n\nAmy Hobbyis an Oscar®-nominated and Emmy Award w
 inning producer with credits on 30+ films. In addition to co-hostingFilms 
 Not Made\, she co-founded Distribution Advocates and the merch-for-films c
 ompany Cutaway.\n\nAvi Zev Weideris a writer/director/producer whose work 
 often lives at the intersection of technology and humanity. He's also a ve
 teran sound supervisor who writes the from-the-set Substack\, The Sound Re
 port.\n\n🎟️ Tickets Available\n\n🔗 https://woodstockfilmfestival.o
 rg/2026-all-events?eventId=6aa1be2c843a0b27c5b431cf
LOCATION:Utopia Studios\, 293 Tinker Street\, Woodstock\, NY 12498
URL:https://woodstockfilmfestival.org/2026-all-events?eventId=6aa1be2c843a
 0b27c5b431cf
END:VEVENT
