BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:New York Women in Film & Television (NYWIFT) - Breaking the Frame 
 - How Far Have Women in Film Really Come? 🎟️
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T143000
DTSTAMP:20260924T205225Z
UID:6aa1be5d4a562fb0e741ea94@woodstockfilmfestival.org
DESCRIPTION:As the film industry continues to evolve\, so too have the opp
 ortunities for women behind and in front of the camera. From the pioneers 
 who opened doors to today’s filmmakers redefining storytelling\, this co
 nversation celebrates how far the industry has come\, the progress being m
 ade\, and the opportunities that lie ahead. Through personal experiences a
 nd industry insights\, leading filmmakers will explore the changing landsc
 ape for women in film\, the conversations that can help move the industry 
 forward\, and how the next generation can continue breaking the frame and 
 creating new possibilities for women in the industry.\n\nPanelists:\n\nRos
 anna Arquette\,Gina Gershon\, & Rachel Grady\n\nRosanna Arquettehas worked
  with world renown directors including Martin Scorsese\, Quentin Tarantino
 \, John Sayles\, Luc Besson\, David Cronenberg\, Hal Ashby\, Allison Ander
 s\, and many more. She most recently finished filmingThe Dizassterstarring
  opposite Lea Thompson and on a Charli XCX-Led FeatureThe Momentopposite A
 lexander Skarsgard. She will next be seen in Amazon’sBallardfor season 2
  opposite Maggie Q. Rosanna can also be seen in Showtime'sThe L Word: Gene
 ration Qand Ryan Murphy's Netflix seriesRatchedalongside Sarah Paulson. Sh
 e also played the female lead in the movieThe Etruscan Smileproduced by Ac
 ademy Award®-winner Arthur Cohn starring alongside Brian Cox.\n\nDebra Gr
 anikis the director of Winter's Bone\, nominated for four Oscars\, includi
 ng Best Picture. Her other films include: Down To The Bone\, Stray Dog\, 
 and Leave No Trace. She has just finished a five-part nonfiction series ca
 lled Conbody Vs Everybody\, shot over the past eight years about the exper
 iences of people reentering New York City after incarceration. Conbody\, r
 eleased in 2026\, premiered on the Criterion Channel and is now available 
 for streaming. Her next project is an adaptation of the non-fiction book\,
  Nickel and Dimed by Barbara Ehrenreich.\n\nIntroduction by:\n\nKim Jackso
 nis a celebrated creative producer and co-founder of Evotion Entertainment
 \, whose work has received Gotham\, Spirit\, and NAACP Award nominations\,
  as well as the Grand Prize at the Deauville Film Festival. Jackson’s fi
 lms have been selected for opening night at New Directors/New Films at MoM
 A\, the London Science Museum\, and featured in competition at several not
 able festivals including Sundance\, Cannes\, Tribeca\, Rotterdam\, Deauvil
 le and Woodstock. Jackson is an active member of the PGA\, the Artist Acad
 emy at Lincoln Center\, Producers United\, Women Independent Producer\, an
 d is currently serving as the Chair of the Board of Directors for New York
  Women in Film & Television.\n\nModerator:\n\nCynthia Lópezis the Chief E
 xecutive Officer of New York Women in Film & Television\, an award-winning
  media strategist\, and former Commissioner of the New York City Mayor’s
  Office of Media and Entertainment where she implemented strategies to sup
 port film and TV production throughout the five boroughs. López is the re
 cipient of many coveted industry awards including: 11 News and Documentary
  Emmy Awards\, the American Documentary: Special Emmy Award for Excellence
  in Documentary Filmmaking\, three Peabody Awards\, and two duPont-Columbi
 a Awards.\n\nPrior to working as Commissioner\, López was Executive Vice 
 President and co-Executive Producer of the award-winning PBS documentary s
 eriesAmerican Documentary | POV\, and was involved in the organization’s
  strategic growth and creative development for 14 years. Her ability to fo
 rge strategic partnerships among corporate and public interest media has b
 een a signature of her work. Notable partnerships include:The New York Tim
 es\, Reuters\, Al-Jazeera Network\, Discovery Communications\, The Moth\, 
 Story Corps\, Harpo Studios and ABC News\,Nightlinewith Ted Koppel. Lopez 
 is proud to have spent her career collaborating with independent filmmaker
 s across all sectors of the film and television industry. She was honored 
 along with Martin Scorsese and Michael Apted\, the Leading Light Award fro
 m DOC NYC’s Visionaries Tribute. She currently serves on several nationa
 l boards\, and is on the distinguished Peabody Awards Board of Jurors.\n\n
 🎟️ Tickets Available\n\n🔗 https://woodstockfilmfestival.org/2026-a
 ll-events?eventId=6aa1be5d4a562fb0e741ea94
LOCATION:Utopia Studios\, 293 Tinker Street\, Woodstock\, NY 12498
URL:https://woodstockfilmfestival.org/2026-all-events?eventId=6aa1be5d4a56
 2fb0e741ea94
END:VEVENT
