DTSTAMP:20260916T171252Z
UID:6aa86c8f153010043a379724@woodstockfilmfestival.org
DESCRIPTION:Women’s tennis changed forever in 1973 when 90 million peopl
 e watched the accomplished Billie Jean King beat an arrogant male chauvini
 st named Bobby Riggs. King’s many sacrifices as she fights for equality 
 for women in sports and in life inspire this remarkable film. – Sabina B
