BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:In Conversation: Tony Goldwyn & Griffin Dunne 🎟️
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T170000
DTSTAMP:20260917T195132Z
UID:6aa1bf4b04d5e95e0b11709a@woodstockfilmfestival.org
DESCRIPTION:Panelists:\n\n﻿TONY GOLDWYN\n\nTony Goldwyncompleted directi
 ng his latest film\,Hello Darkness\, teaming up again with his friend Tony
  Spiridakis who wrote the screenplay. They previously partnered onEzra\,wi
 th Bobby Cannavale and Robert DeNiro. The film won the Grand Jury Prize at
  the Boulder International Film Festival and Audience Awards at the Woodst
 ock and Sun Valley Film Festivals. Goldwyn made his feature directorial de
 but withA Walk on the Moon. The film premiered at the Sundance Film Festiv
 al and received special recognition from the National Board of Review for 
 Excellence in Independent Filmmaking. Additionally\, he directedConviction
 \, starring Hilary Swank and Sam Rockwell\, which earned Swank a SAG Award
  nomination\, won Best Film at the Boston Film Festival and was awarded a 
 Freedom of Expression honor from the National Board of Review.\n\nAs an ac
 tor\, Goldwyn gave a memorable performance as the head of the ‘Christmas
  Adventurers Club’ in Paul Thomas Anderson’s Academy Award®-winning f
 eature\,One Battle After Another.He was also seen in the Academy Award-win
 ning Best PictureOppenheimer\,and the award-winning ensemble ofKing Richar
 dwith Will Smith. Goldwyn is also known for playing Sam’s (Patrick Swayz
 e) best friend and villain Carl Bruner in Jerry Zucker’s blockbuster hit
 Ghost. Currently he stars as DA Nicholas Baxter inLaw & Order\, and was a 
 recurring guest star on the Emmy-winning comedyHacks. Previously he starre
 d as everyone’s favorite President ‘Fitz’ inScandal. Also\, he and h
 is daughter\, Anna Musky-Goldwyn\, have launched a podcast calledFar From 
 the Treewhich looks at other parent/child duos working in the same industr
 y.\n\nGRIFFIN DUNNE\n\nWhile known for starring in such iconic films asAn 
 American Werewolf In Londonand producing and starring in Martin Scorsese's
 After Hours\, Golden Globe Award and Oscar®-nomineeGriffin Dunnehas worke
 d behind and in front of the camera for over 40 years. His acting credits 
 includeThis Is Us\, opposite Mandy Moore and Sterling K. Brown\;Dallas Buy
 ers Club\; and Joey Soloway’s provocative Amazon Studio seriesI Love Dic
 k\, opposite Kevin Bacon and Kathryn Hahn.\n\nDunne started producing at a
 ge 23 withChilly Scenes Of Winter(dir. Joan Silver)\, and followed withBab
 y It’s You(dir. John Sayles)\,Running On Empty(dir. Sidney Lumet)\,Once 
 Around(dir. Lasse Hallström) andWhite Palace(dir. Louis Mandoki). He then
  pivoted to direct and write an Oscar-nominated short calledDuke Of Groove
 . Other directing credits includeAddicted To Lovestarring Meg Ryan\,Practi
 cal Magicstarring Sandra Bullock and Nicole Kidman\,Fierce Peoplestarring 
 Diane Lane and Donald Sutherland\, andThe Center Will Not Holdabout his au
 nt Joan Didion. In 2024 Dunne wrote aNew York Timesbest selling family mem
 oir calledThe Friday Afternoon Club.\n\n🎟️ Tickets Available\n\n🔗 
 https://woodstockfilmfestival.org/2026-all-events?eventId=6aa1bf4b04d5e95e
 0b11709a
LOCATION:Utopia Studios\, 293 Tinker Street\, Woodstock\, NY 12498
URL:https://woodstockfilmfestival.org/2026-all-events?eventId=6aa1bf4b04d5
 e95e0b11709a
END:VEVENT
