BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:In Conversation with Britt Lower 🎟️
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T190000
DTSTAMP:20260921T135154Z
UID:6aa85ed80c61cca506d64c58@woodstockfilmfestival.org
DESCRIPTION:Britt Loweris an Emmy-winning actor\, an artist\, and filmmake
 r. Lower is well known for starring as 'Helly' in the Emmy-nominated Apple
  TV series Severance\, alongside Adam Scott\, Patricia Arquette\, John Tur
 turro\, and Christopher Walken. For her performance in Season 2\, Lower wo
 n the 2025 Emmy Award for “Outstanding Lead Actress in a Drama Series”
  and was nominated for the 2026 Golden Globe Award\, the 2026 Critics' Cho
 ice Award\, and two 2026 Actors Awards. For Season 1\, she received a 2022
  Gotham Award nomination for “Outstanding Performance in a New Series”
  and a 2023 SAG Award nomination for “Outstanding Performance by an Ense
 mble in a Drama Series.” Severance is currently in production on its thi
 rd season. Additionally\, Lower stars in Netflix’s limited series I Will
  Find You\, based on Harlan Coben’s bestselling novel\, opposite Sam Wor
 thington and Milo Ventimiglia. The series is the fifth most-watched Englis
 h\\ Netflix series of all time. At the 2024 Tribeca Film Festival\, Lower 
 starred in Naomi Jaye’s Darkest Miriam (produced by Charlie Kaufman) and
  Tolga Karaçelik’s Psycho Therapy alongside Steve Buscemi and John Maga
 ro\, which won the Audience Award. Among her numerous other features\, Low
 er co-starred in Holly Slept Over\, Sisters\, Mr. Roosevelt\, and Revenge 
 for Jolly! with Oscar Isaac. On television\, she starred in Simon Rich’s
  Man Seeking Woman\; had recurring roles in Casual\, Unforgettable and Fut
 ure Man\; and made notable guest appearances on HBO’s High Maintenance a
 longside Ben Sinclair. Lower made her directorial debut at the 2021 Tribec
 a Film Festival with Circus Person\, a short film she wrote\, produced\, a
 nd starred in. The film follows a painter who joins the circus in the wake
  of heartbreak\, blending live action and animated body paint to explore t
 hemes of healing through radical love. Drawing inspiration from her own ex
 periences performing as a ringmaster in one-ring tent circuses\, Britt is 
 currently developing Circus Person into a feature film. After growing up i
 n rural Illinois\, Lower studied visual art and theater at Northwestern Un
 iversity before moving to New York City. She lives in Brooklyn with her fa
 mily\, including their recently rescued dog named Bowtie. Her husband and 
 her young stepchildren also share her love of the circus world and often p
 erform in their home for friends and family under the name ‘The Extra-Or
 dinary Circus.’\n\nThelma Adamsis a prominent American critic\, an outsp
 oken voice in the Hollywood community\, and a founding participant in the 
 Awards Site GoldDerby.com. A two-time Chair of the New York Film Critics C
 ircle\, she has been the in-house film critic for Us Weekly and The New Yo
 rk Post\, and has written essays\, celebrity profiles and reviews for AARP
 \, The Wrap\, The Boston Globe\, Variety\, Yahoo! Movies\,The New York Tim
 es\, O: The Oprah Magazine\, The Hollywood Reporter\, Parade\, Marie Clair
 e and The Huffington Post. She co-produced the Emmy-nominated Feud: Bette 
 and Joan. Adams studied history at the University of California\, Berkeley
 \, and received her MFA from Columbia University. Thelma Adams is the auth
 or of the best-selling historical novels Bittersweet Brooklyn and The Last
  Woman Standing\, as well as Playdate\, which Oprah magazine described as 
 “a witty debut novel.”\n\n🎟️ Tickets Available\n\n🔗 https://wo
 odstockfilmfestival.org/2026-all-events?eventId=6aa85ed80c61cca506d64c58
LOCATION:Utopia Studios\, 293 Tinker Street\, Woodstock\, NY 12498
URL:https://woodstockfilmfestival.org/2026-all-events?eventId=6aa85ed80c61
 cca506d64c58
END:VEVENT
